<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Merged into the generated bundle Info.plist by tauri-bundler (and used as-is
  by `tauri dev` on macOS).

  Why these keys exist at all: MDReader is NOT sandboxed, but macOS still gates
  ~/Documents, ~/Desktop and ~/Downloads behind the privacy (TCC) layer. When
  the app first opens a folder under one of them, the system raises the consent
  prompt — and the string it shows the user is the matching
  NS*FolderUsageDescription from this file. Without the key there is no sentence
  to show, and the request is far more likely to be refused outright with EPERM
  and no prompt at all, which leaves the user with no route to grant access from
  inside the app.

  Scope note: these are the three user folders a person actually keeps notes in,
  and nothing more. No Full Disk Access, no NSSystemAdministrationUsageDescription,
  no removable volumes. Each key only ever produces a prompt when the user has
  themselves chosen a folder in that location.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>NSDocumentsFolderUsageDescription</key>
	<string>MDReader needs access to your Documents folder to list and read the markdown files in the workspace folder you choose.</string>
	<key>NSDesktopFolderUsageDescription</key>
	<string>MDReader needs access to your Desktop folder to list and read the markdown files in the workspace folder you choose.</string>
	<key>NSDownloadsFolderUsageDescription</key>
	<string>MDReader needs access to your Downloads folder to list and read the markdown files in the workspace folder you choose.</string>
</dict>
</plist>
